{"seeAlsoSections":[{"title":"Related Documentation","anchor":"Related-Documentation","identifiers":["doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/ScreenState","doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/ScreenStateDisplayableError","doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/ScreenStateDefaultErrorView","doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/ScreenStateDefaultErrorUIView","doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/Accessibility"]},{"title":"Error presentation","generated":true,"anchor":"Error-presentation","identifiers":["doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/ScreenStateDisplayableError"]}],"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"content","content":[{"level":2,"text":"Overview","anchor":"Overview","type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":".error"},{"type":"text","text":" is the one state whose presentation can’t be fully generic — a timed-out request, a missing article, and a malformed response all deserve different words, and sometimes a different action, even though they’re all just an "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Error"},{"type":"text","text":" to "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/ScreenStateStore","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":". This article rounds up the three pieces "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/ScreenStateDefaultErrorView","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":"\/"},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/ScreenStateDefaultErrorUIView","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" use to narrow that gap without you writing a fully custom placeholder."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"level":2,"text":"The offline-aware variant","anchor":"The-offline-aware-variant","type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/ScreenState\/isConnectivityError(_:)","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" is "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"true"},{"type":"text","text":" for a "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"URLError"},{"type":"text","text":" indicating no network connectivity ("},{"type":"codeVoice","code":".notConnectedToInternet"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":".networkConnectionLost"},{"type":"text","text":") or a timed-out request ("},{"type":"codeVoice","code":".timedOut"},{"type":"text","text":"). When it’s "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"true"},{"type":"text","text":", the default Error placeholders swap their usual warning-triangle icon and “Something Went Wrong” title for a "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"wifi.exclamationmark"},{"type":"text","text":" icon and “Connection Issue” instead — the same distinction a fully custom placeholder can make with the same check:"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"syntax":"swift","code":["if ScreenState<Never>.isConnectivityError(error) {","    \/\/ show your own offline-specific treatment","}"],"type":"codeListing"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Every other error, including other "},{"code":"URLError","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" codes, falls back to the generic treatment."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"level":2,"text":"The secondary action slot","anchor":"The-secondary-action-slot","type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Both default Error placeholders take an optional "},{"code":"secondaryAction: (title: String, action: () -> Void)?","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" alongside "},{"code":"onRetry","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" — a second button for something other than retrying, like going back to the previous screen instead of hammering a request that’s going to fail the same way again:"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"syntax":"swift","code":["ScreenStateDefaultErrorView(error: error, onRetry: reloa